# Fixture for plus_without_bscb_test (issue #123): what -no-bscb still lets a
# bimolecular rule do inside one complex once the `+` between product
# patterns is tested whatever the flag.
#
# One complex holds an E and an S, another an F and a G, and there is no
# other copy of any of them, so every pair either rule can draw lies inside
# one complex.
#
#   Mod    deletes nothing, so its products come apart only if its reactants
#          did. -no-bscb lets one complex supply both, and Mod then fires:
#          the `+` is a question about what the rule parts, and it parts
#          nothing. (BNG2 never lets one complex supply both reactant
#          patterns, so it has no answer here; this follows NFsim, which
#          lets the rule fire.)
#   Close  makes a bond inside the complex, the ring closure -no-bscb exists
#          to allow. One product pattern, so there is no `+` to test.

begin model
begin parameters
  k  4    # k * t_end = 20: a rule that can fire has fired, but for e^-20
end parameters

begin molecule types
  E(s,b)
  S(p~0~1,e)
  F(x,b)
  G(y,f)
end molecule types

begin seed species
  E(s,b!1).S(p~0,e!1)  1
  F(x,b!1).G(y,f!1)    1
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules Mod_on   S(p~1)
  Molecules Close_on F(x!+)
end observables

begin reaction rules
  Mod:   E(s) + S(p~0) -> E(s) + S(p~1)  k
  Close: F(x) + G(y) -> F(x!1).G(y!1)  k
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
